- Feature to change the color of the highlighted cells;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/36457745/6ee8f3e59bd875cb8cce09dc8922b50d8f1f1386.gif[/img]

- Increased window size in windowed mode;
- Minor bugs fixed.

Three new images have been added to the latest DLC – [b]The Family[/b].

The [b]update 1.3.1[/b] includes the following:
[list]
[*] opportunity to adjust automatic color switch;
[*] automatic color switch is now available in all working area modes (earlier it used to be available only in the full-screen mode);
[*] color sorting on the panel;
[*] hot keys [b]Q[/b] and [b]E[/b] which enable changing the current color.
[/list]
 
The [b]update 1.5.0[/b] will feature the opportunity to modify the color palette and to adjust brightness and working area settings (background color, grid disabling, etc.).

In this update we’ve added:
[list]
[*] indication of saving;
[*] game progress saving by pressing F5 key;
[*] support of a pen;
[*] scrollbar;
[*] scaling icons.
[/list]

The  owners of the top video cards have faced some game stability problems. I suppose that this may be caused by the version of the game engine, so I’ve updated the game engine to the latest version.

[b]The release of the first commercial DLC for this game is postponed for several days and is going to take place on April 26.[/b]

Unfortunately, due to the necessity to solve game malfunction problems, it wasn’t possible to include three new levels in this update. I simply didn’t have enough time to animate and prepare the images for the publication.
[b]The new levels are going to be added in an off-schedule update 1.0.2.1. (April 20-21).[/b]

